             Web & Mobile Listeners

🛠 12. Folder Structure Recommendation
project/
 ├── backend/           # Node.js (Nest/Express)
 │    ├── routes/
 │    ├── controllers/
 │    ├── services/
 │    ├── srs-hooks/    # on-publish, on-unpublish APIs
 │    └── live/         # token generation, live-state
 │
 ├── admin-frontend/    # React admin panel (WebRTC publish UI)
 │
 ├── client-frontend/   # Public website (player)
 │
 ├── liquidsoap/
 │    └── radio.liq     # auto music + fallback
 │
 ├── srs/
 │    └── srs.conf
 │
 └── docker-compose.yml

🎯 13. Key Points to Always Remember

SRS does not generate audio → Liquidsoap does

SRS streams media → WebRTC in → HLS out

Security is done through:

Backend-issued tokens

SRS http_hooks validation

WebRTC ingest always needs:

srsApiUrl (1985)

streamUrl (with token)

HLS is the best for listeners:

Works well on low network

Adaptive bitrate possible

Liquidsoap handles:

Random playlist

Scheduling

Live-switching

🧩 14. Final Master Listener URL

Your entire system outputs one final stream:

http://YOUR_SERVER:8080/live/radio.m3u8


This is the link you give to:

Web player

Mobile app

Smart speakers

Embedded players

Everything else (admin, fallback, auto music) is handled internally.







1️⃣ Detailed Flow – Admin Goes Live from Browser
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        ADMIN BROWSER                         │
│                (React Admin "Go Live" Page)                  │
└───────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                │
                │ 1. Admin logs in with email/password
                │
                ▼
       ┌──────────────────────────────┐
       │       NODE BACKEND          │
       │   /api/auth/login           │
       └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                      │
                      │ 2. Backend verifies credentials,
                      │    issues JWT (admin access token)
                      │
                      ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        ADMIN BROWSER                         │
│         Stores JWT (memory/localStorage/cookie)              │
└───────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                │
                │ 3. Admin clicks "Go Live"
                │    Frontend calls:
                │    GET /api/live/publish-config
                │    Authorization: Bearer <JWT>
                │
                ▼
       ┌──────────────────────────────┐
       │       NODE BACKEND          │
       │   /api/live/publish-config  │
       └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                      │
                      │ 4. Backend:
                      │    - Verifies JWT, role == "admin"
                      │    - Creates short-lived stream token (JWT/UUID)
                      │    - Associates token with:
                      │          app   = "live"
                      │          stream= "admin"
                      │          exp   = NOW + 5 minutes
                      │    - Response:
                      │        {
                      │          streamUrl: "webrtc://SRS_IP/live/admin?token=XYZ",
                      │          srsApiUrl: "http://SRS_IP:1985/rtc/v1/publish"
                      │        }
                      │
                      ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        ADMIN BROWSER                         │
│ 5. Receives streamUrl + srsApiUrl                            │
│    - Requests mic: getUserMedia({ audio:true })              │
│    - Creates RTCPeerConnection                               │
│    - Adds mic track to PeerConnection                        │
│    - Creates SDP offer                                       │
│    - Sends HTTP POST to SRS API:                             │
│                                                              │
│   POST http://SRS_IP:1985/rtc/v1/publish                     │
│   {                                                          │
│     api: "http://SRS_IP:1985/rtc/v1/publish",                │
│     streamurl: "webrtc://SRS_IP/live/admin?token=XYZ",       │
│     sdp: "<offer_sdp>"                                       │
│   }                                                          │
└───────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                │
                │ 6. SRS receives publish request (WebRTC SDP)
                │    Extracts:
                │       app    = "live"
                │       stream = "admin"
                │       param  = "?token=XYZ"
                │
                ▼
       ┌──────────────────────────────┐
       │              SRS            │
       │        (http_hooks)         │
       └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                      │
                      │ 7. SRS triggers http_hook:
                      │
                      │   POST http://BACKEND:3000/api/srs/on-publish
                      │   {
                      │      "action": "on_publish",
                      │      "app": "live",
                      │      "stream": "admin",
                      │      "param": "?token=XYZ",
                      │      "ip": "<admin_ip>"
                      │   }
                      │
                      ▼
       ┌──────────────────────────────┐
       │       NODE BACKEND          │
       │    /api/srs/on-publish      │
       └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                      │
                      │ 8. Backend:
                      │    - Parses param -> token = "XYZ"
                      │    - Validates token:
                      │         * signature (if JWT)
                      │         * expiry
                      │         * app == "live"
                      │         * stream == "admin"
                      │         * tied to this admin user
                      │    - If valid:
                      │         { "code": 0 }
                      │      else:
                      │         { "code": 1, "message": "Unauthorized" }
                      │
                      ▼
       ┌──────────────────────────────┐
       │             SRS             │
       └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                      │
                      │ 9A. If code == 0:
                      │      - Accept WebRTC publish
                      │      - Create stream: app="live", stream="admin"
                      │      - Start receiving RTP audio from browser
                      │      - Start generating HLS:
                      │          http://SRS_IP:8080/live/admin.m3u8
                      │
                      │ 9B. If code != 0:
                      │      - Reject WebRTC publish
                      │      - Close connection to admin
                      │
                      ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        ADMIN BROWSER                         │
│ 10. If accepted:                                             │
│     - setRemoteDescription(answer_sdp from SRS)              │
│     - WebRTC connection established                          │
│     - Admin now streaming live audio → SRS                   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

2️⃣ Detailed Flow – Liquidsoap Fallback (Admin vs Auto-Music)

Here we assume Liquidsoap does stream switching and SRS only sees the final combined stream /live/radio.

                           ┌────────────────────┐
                           │  Music Files (mp3) │
                           │  /radio/music      │
                           └─────────┬──────────┘
                                     │
                         1. Auto playlist, random, schedule
                                     │
                                     ▼
                      ┌───────────────────────────┐
                      │        LIQUIDSOAP         │
                      │  radio.liq script         │
                      └───────────┬───────────────┘
                                  │
                                  │ 2. Define sources:
                                  │
                                  │   admin = input.rtmp("rtmp://SRS/live/admin")
                                  │   music = playlist("/radio/music")
                                  │
                                  │   radio = fallback([admin, music])
                                  │
                                  │ 3. Output combined stream:
                                  │
                                  ▼
                        output.rtmp("rtmp://SRS/live/radio", radio)
                                  │
                                  ▼
                   ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
                   │               SRS                │
                   │         RTMP ingest:             │
                   │        app="live", stream="radio"│
                   │                                  │
                   │ HLS output:                      │
                   │  http://SRS_IP:8080/live/radio.m3u8
                   └──────────────────────────────────┘

How fallback logic works:

When admin is live

Admin → WebRTC → SRS → SRS exposes RTMP/HLS for /live/admin

Liquidsoap’s input.rtmp("rtmp://SRS/live/admin") sees valid live input

fallback([admin, music]) chooses admin as active source

Listeners hear admin voice/music via /live/radio.m3u8

When admin stops

WebRTC connection closes → SRS /live/admin stops

Liquidsoap input for admin becomes offline

fallback([admin, music]) automatically switches to music

Listeners still use /live/radio.m3u8, but now hear auto music

Key point:
👉 Listeners always connect to the same HLS URL (e.g. /live/radio.m3u8).
They never need to switch anything – the switching happens inside Liquidsoap.

3️⃣ Detailed Flow – Listener (Web or Mobile)
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   WEB / MOBILE LISTENER APP                    │
│        (React, Next.js, React Native, etc.)                    │
└───────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                │
                │ 1. App loads home/player screen
                │
                │ 2. Calls backend:
                │
                │   GET /api/live/state
                │
                ▼
       ┌───────────────────────────────────┐
       │           NODE BACKEND           │
       └──────────────────┬────────────────┘
                          │
                          │ 3. Backend checks:
                          │    - Is there a current live session?
                          │      e.g. from Redis/DB flag: station:fm1:isLive
                          │    - What is the public play URL?
                          │      (usually always /live/radio.m3u8)
                          │
                          │  Returns:
                          │    {
                          │      "isLive": true/false,
                          │      "playUrl": "http://SRS_IP:8080/live/radio.m3u8",
                          │      "nowPlaying": { show, title, dj, etc. }
                          │    }
                          │
                          ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   WEB / MOBILE LISTENER APP                    │
│ 4. Receives live state + playUrl                               │
│    - Updates UI:                                               │
│        if isLive: show "🔴 LIVE"                               │
│        else:   show "Auto Music" or "Offline"                  │
│    - Creates HLS audio player:                                 │
│                                                                │
│   <audio controls autoplay                                     │
│          src="http://SRS_IP:8080/live/radio.m3u8">             │
│                                                                │
│   or (React Native):                                           │
│   <Video source={{ uri: playUrl }} ... />                      │
│                                                                │
│ 5. Player requests HLS:                                        │
│                                                                │
│   GET http://SRS_IP:8080/live/radio.m3u8                       │
│   GET http://SRS_IP:8080/live/radio-0.ts  (segments)           │
│   GET http://SRS_IP:8080/live/radio-1.ts                       │
│   ...                                                          │
│                                                                │
└───────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                │
                │ 6. SRS serves playlist + segments
                │    (generated from Liquidsoap RTMP input)
                │
                ▼
       ┌───────────────────────────────────┐
       │                 SRS              │
       │   HLS output for /live/radio     │
       └───────────────────────────────────┘

4️⃣ One Big End-to-End Summary Flow
[Admin Login]
Admin Browser  →  Node Backend (JWT)

[Prepare Live]
Admin Browser  →  /api/live/publish-config (JWT)
                ←  streamUrl (webrtc://SRS/live/admin?token=XYZ)
                    srsApiUrl (http://SRS:1985/rtc/v1/publish)

[Start Live Stream via WebRTC]
Admin Browser  →  POST SRS /rtc/v1/publish (with streamUrl + SDP)
SRS            →  POST Backend /api/srs/on-publish (http_hook)
Backend        →  { "code": 0 } if token valid
SRS            →  Accept WebRTC, create stream live/admin
SRS            →  HLS at /live/admin.m3u8 (optional)
SRS            →  RTMP/HLS used by Liquidsoap as "admin" input

[Auto Music + Fallback]
Liquidsoap     →  Reads mp3 folder, builds playlist
Liquidsoap     →  input.rtmp("rtmp://SRS/live/admin")
Liquidsoap     →  fallback([admin, music])
Liquidsoap     →  RTMP out "rtmp://SRS/live/radio"
SRS            →  HLS out "/live/radio.m3u8"

[Listener Playback]
Web/Mobile     →  GET /api/live/state (to Backend)
Backend        →  { isLive, playUrl: "http://SRS/live/radio.m3u8" }
Web/Mobile     →  HLS requests to SRS
SRS            →  Serves playlist + segments
User hears admin or music depending on Liquidsoap fallback

